# s5_onnx_file_export (off-path)
#
# basis      s4_param_mmap_release peak 2681200 kB; single pool (host):
#   heap:python3.10+0x13cc27          867.0 MB   0.316 of the peak   <- this step: io.BytesIO
#   heap:libc10.so+0x4a675            605.6 MB   0.221               torch tensors
#   heap:libstdc++.so.6.0.30+0xf4979  522.7 MB   0.190               the ONNX protobuf parse
#   anon:[heap]                       481.6 MB   0.175               allocator arena, never a target
#
# object     in-memory ONNX buffer, 867 MB for 433 MB payload (io.BytesIO doubling); exported twice
#            (nn/onnx_converter.py:115-132), the first only for the symbolic registry.
# order      conversion-phase object, hidden until s4 removed the inference hump (earlier attempt
#            off-path/s4_onnx_file_export/: object_conformant=no, -2.7%).
# fix        real file for export (write) and _load_onnx_model (seek, onnx_converter.py:212); first export
#            to a file deleted on close. onnx.load still reads ~433 MB at parse time.
# gate       same exporter, kwargs, two calls, order; same bytes parsed; no generator.
# spill      node-local rootfs (/proc/mounts, logged), tmpfs refused, not mmap'd.
#
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: python3.10+0x13cc27
OMP_NUM_THREADS=8
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,beaver_reveal_inplace_cpu,param_mmap_release_cpu,onnx_file_export_cpu
